# Website publish key

This key pair authenticates to `{{ add_website_publish_user }}`, 
the account an external CI can use to publish public workload images to `{{ inventory_hostname }}`.

Files:

- `{{ add_website_publish_key_path }}` - private key. Copy it into the CI secret.
- `{{ add_website_publish_key_path }}.pub` - public key, authorized for the
  publish account.
- `{{ add_website_readme_path }}` - this file.

The publish account has no sudo, is not in the `docker` group, and owns only
`{{ add_website_project_dir }}/<service>/` and
`{{ add_website_trigger_dir }}`. The compose file and deploy script are
root-owned.

## Key rotation

Every run of the playbook replaces this key pair and revokes the previous CI
key. Copy the new private key into the CI secret after each run. Set
`add_website_publish_key_rotate: false` in the host vars to keep the current
key across runs.

## Fetch the private key

As root on the host:

```bash
ssh root@{{ ansible_host | default(inventory_hostname) }} 'cat {{ add_website_publish_key_path }}'
```

Store the output as a CI secret such as `WEBSITE_PUBLISH_KEY`, then write it in
CI:

```bash
mkdir -p ~/.ssh
printf '%s\n' "$WEBSITE_PUBLISH_KEY" > ~/.ssh/website-publish
chmod 600 ~/.ssh/website-publish
```

## Image contract

CI builds the image. The host never builds. The host accepts an archive only
when it contains the exact tag `{{ add_website_image_prefix }}/<service>:latest`
and the image labels `com.co3d.service=public` and
`com.co3d.service.name=<service>`.

```bash
# in CI, exact tag and labels matter
docker buildx build --platform linux/amd64 --load \
  --label com.co3d.service=public \
  --label com.co3d.service.name=website \
  -t {{ add_website_image_prefix }}/website:latest .
docker save {{ add_website_image_prefix }}/website:latest | zstd -T0 -3 > website.tar.zst
sha256sum website.tar.zst > website.tar.zst.sha256
```

Replace `website` appropriately. The image must listen on the
port Caddy routes to (`website` 80, `lobby` 8080).

`<service>.tar.zst.sha256` is optional. If present, the host verifies it before
loading.

## Publish

```bash
rsync -az --delete --chmod=D755,F644 \
  -e 'ssh -i ~/.ssh/website-publish -o IdentitiesOnly=yes -o StrictHostKeyChecking=accept-new' \
  website.tar.zst website.tar.zst.sha256 \
  {{ add_website_publish_user }}@{{ ansible_host | default(inventory_hostname) }}:{{ add_website_project_dir }}/website/

ssh -i ~/.ssh/website-publish -o IdentitiesOnly=yes \
  {{ add_website_publish_user }}@{{ ansible_host | default(inventory_hostname) }} \
  'touch {{ add_website_trigger_dir }}/website.restart'
```

The marker filename is the compose service name. One marker deploys one
service. The host consumes the marker before loading, so a bad archive cannot
hot-loop.

## Verify

```bash
ssh -i ~/.ssh/website-publish {{ add_website_publish_user }}@{{ ansible_host | default(inventory_hostname) }} \
  'ls -la {{ add_website_project_dir }}/website {{ add_website_trigger_dir }}'
```

On the host:

```bash
sudo tail -f {{ add_website_log_file }}
sudo docker compose -f {{ add_website_compose_file }} ps
```

A successful publish logs `loading`, `restarting`, and `deploy complete`.

## Manual restart

Restart the currently loaded image without uploading an archive:

```bash
cd {{ add_website_project_dir }} && sudo docker compose up -d --no-deps lobby
```

## Rollback

Every successful publish prunes the previous public images. There is no image
rollback on the host. Roll back by republishing the previous commit's archive.

## Publishing security model

The publish account (`{{ add_website_publish_user }}`) has no sudo, is not in
the `docker` group, and owns only the artifact and trigger directories.

Publishing does not execute build instructions on this host. CI sends a
finished image archive; the host verifies its checksum when one is provided,
loads it, checks the `com.co3d.service` labels, and restarts the container.

The publish key still controls the code that runs. Treat it as permission to
run arbitrary code in a container. Keep the key in CI secrets only, and rotate it after any suspicion.
